Explicit register operands must appear **at the end of the `asm!` operand list**, after all other operands. They cannot be referenced with `{}` placeholders; write the register name directly in the assembly template.

For example:

```rust
unsafe {
    asm!(
        "mul {}",
        in(reg) a,                  // positional operand first
        inlateout("rax") b => lo,   // explicit register operands last
        lateout("rdx") hi,
    );
}
```

They also cannot precede positional operands; otherwise the compiler reports that positional arguments cannot follow explicit register arguments.
